{"name":"One Year of Rain","hex":"#29465b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"one","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["NATO & ICAO radiotelephony clear code (spelling-alphabet name) for the digit 1."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Oneida."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/one"},{"term":"year","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A period of time akin to the time taken for the Earth to undergo a full cycle of seasons.","The time taken for the Earth to return to the same position along the ecliptic, completing a full cycle of seasons; a tropical year or solar year."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Pronunciation spelling of here.","Pronunciation spelling of hear."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/year"},{"term":"rain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Condensed water falling from a cloud.","Any matter moving or falling, usually through air, and especially if liquid or otherwise figuratively identifiable with raindrops."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have rain fall from the sky.","To fall as or like rain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rain"}],"entries":[{"title":"One Year","blocks":[{"text":"One Year is the debut solo studio album by English singer-songwriter Colin Blunstone, a member of the Zombies. It was released by Epic Records in 1971. It includes \"Say You Don't Mind\", which peaked at number 15 on the UK Singles Chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3d/One_Year_Colin_Blunstone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_Year"},{"title":"1","blocks":[{"text":"1 is a number, numeral, and grapheme. It is the first and smallest positive integer of the infinite sequence of natural numbers. This fundamental property has led to its unique uses in other fields, ranging from science to sports, where it commonly denotes the first, leading, or top thing in a group. 1 is the unit of counting or measurement, and represents a single thing. The representation of 1 evolved from ancient Sumerian and Babylonian symbols to the modern Arabic numeral. Linguistically, in English, \"one\" is a determiner for singular nouns and a gender-neutral pronoun."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1"},{"title":"Year","blocks":[{"text":"A year is a unit of time based on how long it takes the Earth to orbit the Sun. In scientific use, the tropical year and the sidereal year are more exact. The modern calendar year, as reckoned according to the Gregorian calendar, approximates the tropical year by using a system of leap years."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Solar_system_orrery_inner_planets.gif/330px-Solar_system_orrery_inner_planets.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Year"},{"title":"Rain","blocks":[{"text":"Rain or rainfall is a form of atmospheric precipitation composed of droplets of water aerosols that have condensed from atmospheric water vapor and fall by gravity. Depending on the intensity, rain can be described as a drizzle, a shower, a cloudburst or a downpour. It is also often accompanied by other weather phenomena such as strong wind (rainstorm) and lightning (thunderstorm), and may be mixed with hail/ice pellet, snow (sleet) and sandstorm. Rain is a major component of the water cycle and is responsible for depositing most of the fresh water on Earth. It provides water for hydroelectric power plants, crop irrigation, and suitable conditions for many types of ecosystems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg/330px-Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Woodstock_typewriter%2C_1940s%2C_daylight_-_keyboard.jpg/500px-Woodstock_typewriter%2C_1940s%2C_daylight_-_keyboard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Woodstock_typewriter%2C_1940s%2C_daylight_-_keyboard.jpg/1280px-Woodstock_typewriter%2C_1940s%2C_daylight_-_keyboard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Woodstock_typewriter%2C_1940s%2C_daylight_-_keyboard.jpg/500px-Woodstock_typewriter%2C_1940s%2C_daylight_-_keyboard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWoodstock_typewriter%2C_1940s%2C_daylight_-_keyboard.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Clock_24_J.jpg/500px-Clock_24_J.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Clock_24_J.jpg/1280px-Clock_24_J.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Clock_24_J.jpg/500px-Clock_24_J.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The 24-hour tower clock in Venice, using J as a symbol for 1","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClock_24_J.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Konvektionsregen.jpg/500px-Konvektionsregen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Konvektionsregen.jpg/500px-Konvektionsregen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Convective precipitation","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKonvektionsregen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/St